From: Stephan WEGENER <steph.wegener@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:25:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/25] [Onyx] The compositor's tiles rasterised on the Pi's
 other cores

Onyx's POSIX threads all run on core 0; another core is an "app core" (kapi core_acquire /
core_run), whose code makes no kernel call. The compositor now paints in two passes: the main
thread records each dirty rectangle once into an SkPicture, and jobs of at most 512 x 256 pixels
replay it into the tiles' buffers on up to two app cores and on the main thread (pure Skia
there: no WTF, no WebCore); the uploads and the composite stay on the main thread. Small paints
(under 64k pixels), or no free core, keep the direct path. Shared/onyx/OnyxCores.h is the
interface (tools/webkit/onyxcores.c in Onyx: the workers, their own TLS, the RPC served while a
batch runs, the watch on a core that faults or stalls -- its jobs are done again on the main
thread and the process goes on single-threaded). The cores are given back after 10 s without
raster. A self-test (OnyxCoreTest.cpp: eleven stages on a core, then the page's first jobs one
at a time).

Switches (files in SD:/etc): web-gpu-nocores, web-gpu-mainwaits, web-gpu-coretest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
